course: dictionary
lesson: 11771
title: Everyday words at home
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bathrobe is a long, loose coat made of soft towelling or cotton. You wear it before or after a bath or shower to stay warm and dry.
explain: You can see bathrobes at swimming pools and in hotels. «Dad put on his fluffy bathrobe after his shower.» The word fluffy tells you the bathrobe is soft and cosy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The hotel gave every guest a soft white bathrobe.» Hotels, soft, white and a warm coat for after a wash all point to the same meaning, so you can work it out from the context.
fact: A bathrobe is a long, loose coat made of soft towelling or cotton.
fact: «Bathrobe» is a noun, and its plural is «bathrobes».
fact: People wear a bathrobe before or after a bath or shower, and in a story it often means someone is just out of bed or relaxing.
fact: In American English, «bathrobe» can also mean any dressing gown worn around the house.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning: «She wrapped herself in a warm coat after her shower» still makes sense.
exercise: «Dad wrapped himself in his fluffy bathrobe after his shower.» What is a bathrobe? | A swimming costume | *A long, loose coat of soft towelling, worn before or after a bath | A small towel for drying hair | A pair of thick socks for cold feet
exercise: «The hotel gave every guest a soft white bathrobe.» Where would you most likely find this bathrobe? | In a school bus | In a shop window | On a mountain | *In a hotel
exercise: Lily stepped out of the pool and pulled on her bathrobe. Why do you think she wore it? | To go to school | *To keep warm and dry after swimming | To cook dinner | To play football
test: «Still in his bathrobe, Sam made himself toast.» What does this sentence suggest Sam was doing? | *Just out of bed or relaxing at home | Swimming in the sea | Going to a wedding | Running a marathon
test: Which material is a bathrobe usually made of? | Metal | Paper | Glass | *Soft towelling or cotton
exam: What is a bathrobe usually worn for? | *Before or after a bath or shower | Climbing a hill | Cooking dinner | Playing in the snow
